{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba docs/releases/TEMPLATE-checklist.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Release checklist — <tag>\n     2\t\n     3\tCopy this file to `docs/releases/<tag>-checklist.md` before publishing the GitHub Release.\n     4\t`scripts/release-readiness.ts` (run by the release train's readiness job, R3) requires this\n     5\tfile to exist for the tag with **zero unchecked boxes** — every `- [ ]` below is a pre-flight\n     6\titem that must be `- [x]` before the Release is published. The plain \"post\" bullets are\n     7\tverification steps after the train runs; they are deliberately not checkboxes.\n     8\t\n     9\t## Pre-flight (all boxes checked before publishing the Release)\n    10\t\n    11\t- [ ] Version PR merged to main (dispatch `version-pr.yml` → review → merge; ADR-0325):\n    12\t      `.changeset/` drained, versions bumped, CHANGELOGs written, `bun.lock` refreshed, AND\n    13\t      `registry/{ledger.jsonl,index.json,tarballs.json}` updated in the SAME commit\n    14\t- [ ] The draft GitHub Release's tag targets the version-PR merge commit or its\n    15\t      attestation-only successor (docs/audit/checklist only — no package bytes; readiness\n    16\t      reads the R4 audit + this checklist from the TAGGED tree, and this checklist is only\n    17\t      completable after the merge, so a successor commit is the normal shape — operator lock\n    18\t      2026-07-12, first ride). publish.yml re-verifies ancestry and byte-reproduces every\n    19\t      tarball hash at the tag — a mismatch stops the train\n    20\t- [ ] CI green on the release SHA (check · standards-gate · registry-index · oscal-conformance ·\n    21\t      deterministic · support-bot · runtime-images-gate — the push-to-main run on the version-PR merge commit)\n    22\t- [ ] `bun run sot` green\n    23\t- [ ] R4 fresh full audit of the cumulative diff since the last release tag, on file at\n    24\t      `outputs/audit/release-audit-<tag>.md` (SHIP-audit lane: gw-code-reviewer +\n    25\t      gw-security-auditor, findings adversarially verified)\n    26\t- [ ] Live-hybrid retrieval golden leg green locally:\n    27\t      `bun scripts/release-readiness.ts --tag <tag> --local` (Kickoff-M picker lock 2026-07-10:\n    28\t      this leg gates release readiness, not PR CI)\n    29\t- [ ] Site surfaces current: /updates entry drafted, pricing/marketplace copy true-to-built\n    30\t- [ ] Release notes written on the draft GitHub Release (buyer-facing, no ADR citations)\n    31\t- [ ] No open P0/P1 against the buyer install path (registry tarballs resolve for\n    32\t      `dist-tags.latest` of every published package)\n    33\t\n    34\t## R4 artifact schema (R359 / CR-06)\n    35\t\n    36\tThe audit file must begin with strict YAML frontmatter containing only: schema_version: 1,\n    37\tstatus: clean, critical: 0, base (previous release tag), tag (this release), sha (the exact\n    38\t40-character final candidate SHA), reviewed_scope (a non-empty array of paths), and reviewers.\n    39\tReviewers contains exactly one code_review and one security_audit entry; each has role,\n    40\tidentity (non-empty), and reviewed_at (an ISO timestamp with timezone). Unknown fields, failed\n    41\tverdicts, incomplete identities, empty scope and mismatched bindings fail closed. The gate\n    42\tderives the previous release from the candidate's parent history; it never trusts the audit\n    43\tfile to choose its own comparison base. Prose follows the closing frontmatter delimiter.\n    44\t\n    45\tDo not copy a preparation or failed report to the tag-named path. Produce the actual completed\n    46\taudit for the final candidate; the existence of this template is not an attestation.\n    47\t\n    48\t## Post-release verification (after the train completes)\n    49\t\n    50\t- (post) Registry spot-check: `bun add @caisson/kernel@latest` from a clean env with the\n    51\t  standing test license — installs clean\n    52\t- (post) Mirror spot-check: caisson-sh/caisson-oss HEAD carries the release content, history\n    53\t  APPENDED (never rewritten)\n    54\t- (post) npm spot-check: `bunx @caisson-sh/cli@latest --help` resolves the new version\n    55\t- (post) Site redeploy live: /updates shows the entry\n    56\t- (post) Announcement posted (operator act — W3/window motion per ADR-0318 F5)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
