{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba packages/tool-exec/README.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# @caisson/tool-exec\n     2\t\n     3\tGoverned tool-call / sandboxed-exec primitive — the security floor Agentic-Dev's tool layer stands\n     4\ton.\n     5\t\n     6\t## What it gives you\n     7\t\n     8\t- **Default-deny command allowlist.** `createToolExec({ allowlist })` — a call names a registered\n     9\t  logical command; anything unregistered (or an empty allowlist) is refused with a `NotFoundError`\n    10\t  before anything spawns.\n    11\t- **`execFile` arg-arrays only.** Never `execSync`/`exec`/`shell: true`, never a concatenated\n    12\t  command string. Each registered command declares a real executable + a Zod-`.strict()` schema its\n    13\t  args must satisfy; args are validated with `parseStrict` and the VALIDATED result becomes the\n    14\t  argv array passed to `execFile` — no user/agent value ever reaches a shell.\n    15\t- **Structured argument provenance.** Every call returns `{ command, args, exitCode, stdout,\n    16\tstderr, ok, reason?, at }` — a plain-data audit record (not WORM), with output bounded to 64KB.\n    17\t- **Injected everything.** `cwd`, `timeoutMs`, the spawn seam (`execFn`), and the clock (`now`) are\n    18\t  all config — no module-level secrets/constants for endpoints or executables.\n    19\t- **Optional per-command `env`.** A `CommandSpec` may set `env: { … }` to narrow the spawned\n    20\t  child's environment. Absent (the default), the child inherits the parent's full environment —\n    21\t  unchanged from before this option existed. When supplied, the object is used verbatim (never\n    22\t  merged with `process.env`), so include `PATH` explicitly if the command needs it. A default flip\n    23\t  to always-narrow would be a separate major version.\n    24\t\n    25\t## Entry points\n    26\t\n    27\t- `.` — the full surface, node-capable (`createToolExec` and its `execFile` spawn seam).\n    28\t- `./browser` — the browser-safe subset: `createToolProposer`, the default-deny lookup + Zod argv\n    29\t  validation with no spawn attached, so the gate can decide inside a client bundle. It is the same\n    30\t  implementation `createToolExec` runs. Every name on `./browser` is also on `.`.\n    31\t\n    32\t## Use\n    33\t\n    34\t```ts\n    35\timport { z } from \"zod\";\n    36\timport { createToolExec } from \"@caisson/tool-exec\";\n    37\t\n    38\tconst toolExec = createToolExec({\n    39\t  allowlist: [\n    40\t    {\n    41\t      name: \"git-status\",\n    42\t      command: \"/usr/bin/git\",\n    43\t      argsSchema: z.array(z.string()).max(1).default([\"status\"]),\n    44\t    },\n    45\t  ],\n    46\t  cwd: \"/repo\",\n    47\t  timeoutMs: 30_000,\n    48\t});\n    49\t\n    50\tconst result = await toolExec.run(\"git-status\", [\"status\"], \"agent-turn-14\");\n    51\t// result.ok / result.exitCode / result.stdout / result.args (the resolved argv array)\n    52\t```\n    53\t\n    54\tA name not on the allowlist, or args that fail the schema, throw before any process spawns.\n    55\t\n    56\t## Tests\n    57\t\n    58\t`bun test packages/tool-exec/src` — default-deny (unregistered name, empty allowlist),\n    59\tschema-rejects-before-exec, a valid call's full provenance record, a non-zero exit captured (not\n    60\tthrown), and one real `execFile` spawn against `node -e` proving the bounded-output path end to end.\n    61\t\n    62\t## Two-phase approvals (ADR-0423)\n    63\t\n    64\t`await tool.propose(name, input, reason)` returns a serializable `ToolApproval`:\n    65\trandom approval ID, canonical digest, policy version, command, validated argv and reason.\n    66\tKeep the `ToolExec` instance and its record store on the trusted server. Only call\n    67\t`execute(approval)` after your application authenticates and authorizes the approval\n    68\tactor; the package does not implement that actor's authentication or approval UI.\n    69\t\n    70\tExecution atomically consumes the private record, checks the public digest, revalidates\n    71\tthe saved original input with the current schema, and requires the resulting argv to\n    72\tmatch what was approved. Command, explicit environment or `policyVersion` rotation\n    73\tinvalidates outstanding records. Environment is never accepted in the public envelope.\n    74\tThe ADR-0420 inherited-environment default remains unchanged when a spec omits `env`.\n    75\t\n    76\tThe default store snapshots input and holds at most 1,000 pending records in memory;\n    77\trestart loses pending approvals. For persistence, inject `approvalStore` implementing\n    78\tcreate-only `put` and atomic get-and-delete `consume`; never expose either to clients.\n    79\tA digest is an integrity binding to this trusted record, not a signature over arbitrary\n    80\tclient data. Invalid or rotated execution attempts consume the record once its ID is\n    81\tresolved; request a new proposal after rejection. `createToolProposer` remains a pure\n    82\tbrowser-safe validation preview; its `ProposedToolCall` cannot be passed to `execute`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba knowledge/decisions/ADR-0424-recheck-cart-entitlements-before-checkout.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba knowledge/decisions/ADR-0424-recheck-cart-entitlements-before-checkout.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# ADR-0424 — Recheck cart entitlements before checkout\n     2\t\n     3\t- Date: 2026-09-16\n     4\t- Status: Accepted — operator R359 / EST-ASK-317\n     5\t- Scope: site cart ownership and multi-item checkout\n     6\t- Supersedes: ADR-0418 optional-hint absence short-circuit for cart ownership\n     7\t\n     8\t## Context\n     9\t\n    10\tCR-03 showed that a valid durable Better Auth session can outlive an independently\n    11\tabsent, evicted or expired hint cookie. Treating hint absence as signed-out hides active\n    12\townership, and client-side Paddle line submission did not recheck those entitlements.\n    13\t\n    14\t## Decision\n    15\t\n    16\tThe owned-items endpoint always resolves the real Better Auth session. Hint presence or\n    17\tabsence has no effect on ownership. Checkout moves to an authenticated, same-origin JSON\n    18\tserver endpoint. It derives account identity from that session, validates a bounded strict\n    19\tlist of catalog IDs, resolves current server catalog price IDs, deduplicates lines and reads\n    20\tactive entitlements in the same tenant scope before contacting Paddle. Already-owned exact\n    21\tSKUs are removed; an all-owned cart returns 409 without creating a transaction. Failed reads\n    22\tblock checkout. Account IDs, prices and quantities are not accepted from the client.\n    23\t\n    24\tThe server creates an automatically collected Paddle transaction containing only retained\n    25\tlines and the verified account's custom_data.account_id. Promo codes resolve to active,\n    26\tcheckout-enabled Paddle discounts; unknown/private codes fail without silently charging full\n    27\tprice. Paddle enforces expiry, applicability and redemption limits when applying the discount.\n    28\tThe browser opens only the returned transaction ID and tells the buyer when owned lines were\n    29\tremoved. It clears the cart only after checkout.completed.\n    30\t\n    31\t## Consequences and boundaries\n    32\t\n    33\tThe site runtime requires PADDLE_API_KEY with transaction-write and discount-read permissions\n    34\tfor this cart path; configuration/permission errors fail closed. No credentials or deployment\n    35\tare changed by this repair. PADDLE_ENV selects the same API environment as the existing cancel\n    36\tpath and must agree with NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_ENV at deployment.\n    37\t\n    38\tThis closes the stale client ownership path for exact active SKU grants, preserving the\n    39\texisting ownership semantics: implicit bundle coverage is not newly expanded. Entitlements\n    40\tare checked at transaction creation, not atomically with later payment settlement. Previously\n    41\topened transactions and concurrent independent purchases remain outside this preflight's\n    42\tguarantee. Subscription/single-item flows are unchanged; this lock covers the cart path in CR-03.\n    43\tNo live Paddle request is part of the verification; tests use real Better Auth in-memory sessions\n    44\tand injected entitlement/provider seams, plus server/client binding contracts and mutations.\n    45\t\n    46\tAPI references checked during implementation:\n    47\t\n    48\t- https://developer.paddle.com/api-reference/transactions/create-transaction/\n    49\t- https://developer.paddle.com/api-reference/discounts/list-discounts/\n    50\t- https://developer.paddle.com/paddle-js/methods/paddle-checkout-open/\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba apps/site/lib/auth-server.ts'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba apps/site/lib/auth-server.ts'","aggregated_output":"     1\t// The better-auth sign-in runtime (ADR-0015: better-auth is the self-hosted SessionProvider that\n     2\t// owns its user/session/account/verification tables). This is the SERVER instance the Next route\n     3\t// handler mounts and the dashboard resolves sessions from. It is built LAZILY and is boot/build\n     4\t// safe: with no `DATABASE_URL` + `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` it returns `null` (sign-in simply\n     5\t// unavailable — dev/CI/build with no Postgres), never throwing at import so `next build` and\n     6\t// `bunx tsc` stay green without a live database.\n     7\t//\n     8\t// Auth methods:\n     9\t//  - Magic link (PRIMARY, always on): the link email is sent through `@caisson/email`'s `Emailer`\n    10\t//    port — the Resend driver in prod (`RESEND_API_KEY`), the in-memory capture driver otherwise.\n    11\t//  - Email + password: a signed-up password account requires email verification before it can\n    12\t//    sign in (`requireEmailVerification`) — unlike the magic link, a password alone never proves\n    13\t//    inbox ownership, so the trust boundary needs the extra round trip. Both the verification and\n    14\t//    password-reset emails route through the SAME injected `Emailer`.\n    15\t//  - GitHub + Google OAuth: offered ONLY when their credentials are present (`resolveSocialProviders`).\n    16\t//\n    17\t// The session cookie is hardened per the security floor: `SameSite=Strict`, `HttpOnly`, and\n    18\t// `Secure` (better-auth sets Secure automatically in production). OAuth's short-lived state\n    19\t// cookies keep better-auth's default `SameSite=Lax` — they MUST survive the provider's top-level\n    20\t// cross-site redirect back to our callback, which a Strict cookie would drop; only the durable\n    21\t// SESSION cookie is pinned to Strict.\n    22\timport { createPgPool } from \"@caisson/tenancy-rls\";\n    23\timport type { Pool } from \"pg\";\n    24\timport { betterAuth } from \"better-auth\";\n    25\timport { createAuthMiddleware } from \"better-auth/api\";\n    26\timport { magicLink } from \"better-auth/plugins\";\n    27\timport type { BetterAuthOptions } from \"better-auth/types\";\n    28\t// ADR-0366: better-auth exposes no public `database`-construction subpath (its own internal\n    29\t// `getAdapter` reaches into this same package), so the session-token wrap depends on it\n    30\t// directly, pinned to better-auth's OWN exact version below — the two ship in lockstep upstream.\n    31\timport {\n    32\t  createKyselyAdapter,\n    33\t  kyselyAdapter,\n    34\t} from \"@better-auth/kysely-adapter\";\n    35\timport {\n    36\t  type CaptureEmailer,\n    37\t  type Emailer,\n    38\t  createCaptureEmailer,\n    39\t  createResendEmailer,\n    40\t} from \"@caisson/email\";\n    41\timport { resolveSocialProviders } from \"./auth-config.ts\";\n    42\timport { SESSION_HINT_COOKIE_NAME } from \"./session-hint-cookie.ts\";\n    43\timport { wrapSessionAdapter } from \"./session-adapter.ts\";\n    44\t\n    45\texport { SESSION_HINT_COOKIE_NAME } from \"./session-hint-cookie.ts\";\n    46\t\n    47\t/** The prefixed session cookie name the security floor pins (`${cookiePrefix}.session_token`). */\n    48\texport const SESSION_COOKIE_NAME = \"caisson.session_token\";\n    49\t\n    50\t/** Legacy HttpOnly hint mint/clear compatibility (ADR-0418). ADR-0424 removes the ownership\n    51\t * short-circuit: this cookie never establishes session absence or controls checkout. */\n    52\tconst sessionHintCookieHook = createAuthMiddleware(async (ctx) => {\n    53\t  if (ctx.context.newSession) {\n    54\t    // Unconditionally Secure (unlike the real session cookie, which only forces it in production —\n    55\t    // see `advanced.cookies.session_token` below): this cookie carries no secret, so there's no\n    56\t    // production/dev split to preserve, and modern browsers exempt `localhost` from the\n    57\t    // https-only restriction on Secure cookies, so local dev keeps working.\n    58\t    ctx.setCookie(SESSION_HINT_COOKIE_NAME, \"1\", {\n    59\t      secure: true,\n    60\t      sameSite: \"strict\",\n    61\t      httpOnly: true,\n    62\t      path: \"/\",\n    63\t      expires: ctx.context.newSession.session.expiresAt,\n    64\t    });\n    65\t  } else if (ctx.path === \"/sign-out\") {\n    66\t    // Fail-open in the other direction: a stray hint cookie left behind by a client that ignored\n    67\t    // this Set-Cookie just costs one wasted `/api/cart/owned` fetch (the provider's own fail-open\n    68\t    // contract), never a false \"owned\" marking.\n    69\t    ctx.setCookie(SESSION_HINT_COOKIE_NAME, \"\", {\n    70\t      secure: true,\n    71\t      sameSite: \"strict\",\n    72\t      httpOnly: true,\n    73\t      path: \"/\",\n    74\t      maxAge: 0,\n    75\t    });\n    76\t  }\n    77\t});\n    78\t\n    79\t/**\n    80\t * Resolve the magic-link transport: the Resend driver when `RESEND_API_KEY` is configured, an\n    81\t * in-memory capture driver otherwise (so a dev/CI instance never hits the network and tests can\n    82\t * assert the sent link). The `from` address is env-driven (`RESEND_FROM`) with a safe default —\n    83\t * never a hardcoded secret. Replies to the no-reply sender land in the support inbox.\n    84\t */\n    85\tfunction resolveEmailer(): Emailer | CaptureEmailer {\n    86\t  const apiKey = process.env.RESEND_API_KEY?.trim();\n    87\t  if (apiKey !== undefined && apiKey.length > 0) {\n    88\t    return createResendEmailer({\n    89\t      apiKey,\n    90\t      from: process.env.RESEND_FROM?.trim() ?? \"Caisson <no-reply@caisson.sh>\",\n    91\t      replyTo: \"support@caisson.sh\",\n    92\t    });\n    93\t  }\n    94\t  return createCaptureEmailer();\n    95\t}\n    96\t\n    97\t/**\n    98\t * Build a better-auth instance over a Postgres pool. Exported so tests can construct an instance\n    99\t * against an in-memory database with a capture transport, exercising the real magic-link →\n   100\t * session flow without a live Postgres. `emailer` is injected; `baseURL` is optional (better-auth\n   101\t * infers it from the request when absent).\n   102\t *\n   103\t * `hmacKey` (ADR-0366) is REQUIRED and checked here too (construction-time fail-closed), not just\n   104\t * by `getAuth()`'s env read below — any other caller that forgets it gets the same loud throw\n   105\t * instead of a silent raw-token fallback. The session-token adapter wrap (`session-adapter.ts`)\n   106\t * is built from the SAME `database` here via `createKyselyAdapter`/`kyselyAdapter` (the exact\n   107\t * dialect-detection better-auth itself uses internally), so it works against both a real `pg.Pool`\n   108\t * (production) and the in-memory `bun:sqlite` double used by this app's own tests — a hand-rolled\n   109\t * `PostgresDialect` would only work against the former and break the latter.\n   110\t *\n   111\t * NOTE for callers that also run `getMigrations(auth.options)` (schema DDL, e.g.\n   112\t * `deploy-migrate.ts`): `auth.options.database` below is the WRAPPED adapter FACTORY, which\n   113\t * `getMigrations`'s own dialect detection cannot introspect (it only recognizes a raw\n   114\t * Pool/Dialect/Kysely shape). Substitute the raw `database` value back in for that call:\n   115\t * `getMigrations({ ...auth.options, database })`. Schema DDL is unaffected by the session-token\n   116\t * wrap either way — this is purely about `createKyselyAdapter`'s dialect-detection reach.\n   117\t */\n   118\texport async function createAuth(params: {\n   119\t  database: Pool;\n   120\t  secret: string;\n   121\t  emailer: Emailer;\n   122\t  hmacKey: string;\n   123\t  baseURL?: string | undefined;\n   124\t}) {\n   125\t  const { database, secret, emailer, baseURL, hmacKey } = params;\n   126\t  if (hmacKey.trim().length === 0) {\n   127\t    throw new Error(\n   128\t      \"SESSION_TOKEN_HMAC_KEY is required to construct the auth runtime (ADR-0366) — refusing to start rather than fall back to storing raw session tokens.\",\n   129\t    );\n   130\t  }\n   131\t  // Safe partial cast: `createKyselyAdapter` reads only `config.database` (verified against\n   132\t  // `@better-auth/kysely-adapter`'s source) — the rest of `BetterAuthOptions` is irrelevant to\n   133\t  // dialect detection.\n   134\t  const { kysely, databaseType, transaction } = await createKyselyAdapter({\n   135\t    database,\n   136\t  } as BetterAuthOptions);\n   137\t  if (!kysely) {\n   138\t    throw new Error(\n   139\t      \"session-adapter: failed to initialize the database adapter for the ADR-0366 session-token wrap.\",\n   140\t    );\n   141\t  }\n   142\t  const baseAdapterFactory = kyselyAdapter(kysely, {\n   143\t    type: databaseType ?? \"postgres\",\n   144\t    transaction,\n   145\t  });\n   146\t  return betterAuth({\n   147\t    database: (options: BetterAuthOptions) =>\n   148\t      wrapSessionAdapter(baseAdapterFactory(options), hmacKey),\n   149\t    secret,\n   150\t    basePath: \"/api/auth\",\n   151\t    ...(baseURL !== undefined && baseURL.length > 0 ? { baseURL } : {}),\n   152\t    plugins: [\n   153\t      magicLink({\n   154\t        // PRIMARY sign-in. The link is emailed through the injected transport; the URL better-auth\n   155\t        // generates carries the one-time token and the post-verify redirect (callbackURL).\n   156\t        sendMagicLink: async ({ email, url }): Promise<void> => {\n   157\t          await emailer.send({\n   158\t            to: email,\n   159\t            template: \"magic-link\",\n   160\t            data: { url },\n   161\t          });\n   162\t        },\n   163\t      }),\n   164\t    ],\n   165\t    emailAndPassword: {\n   166\t      enabled: true,\n   167\t      // A password alone doesn't prove inbox ownership the way a clicked magic link does —\n   168\t      // require verification before a password account can sign in.\n   169\t      requireEmailVerification: true,\n   170\t      sendResetPassword: async ({ user, url }): Promise<void> => {\n   171\t        await emailer.send({\n   172\t          to: user.email,\n   173\t          template: \"password-reset\",\n   174\t          data: { url },\n   175\t        });\n   176\t      },\n   177\t    },\n   178\t    emailVerification: {\n   179\t      sendVerificationEmail: async ({ user, url }): Promise<void> => {\n   180\t        await emailer.send({\n   181\t          to: user.email,\n   182\t          template: \"verify-email\",\n   183\t          data: { url },\n   184\t        });\n   185\t      },\n   186\t      sendOnSignUp: true,\n   187\t      autoSignInAfterVerification: true,\n   188\t    },\n   189\t    socialProviders: resolveSocialProviders(process.env),\n   190\t    // ADR-0418: mint/refresh the HttpOnly hint cookie alongside every real session\n   191\t    // create/refresh, clear it on sign-out. See `sessionHintCookieHook` above.\n   192\t    hooks: { after: sessionHintCookieHook },\n   193\t    advanced: {\n   194\t      cookiePrefix: \"caisson\",\n   195\t      cookies: {\n   196\t        session_token: {\n   197\t          // Security floor: the durable session cookie is Strict + HttpOnly. `Secure` is added by\n   198\t          // better-auth in production (NODE_ENV=production).\n   199\t          attributes: { sameSite: \"strict\", httpOnly: true, path: \"/\" },\n   200\t        },\n   201\t      },\n   202\t    },\n   203\t  });\n   204\t}\n   205\t\n   206\ttype AuthInstance = Awaited<ReturnType<typeof createAuth>>;\n   207\t\n   208\t// `undefined` = not yet resolved this process; a resolved promise carries `null` for\n   209\t// resolved-but-unavailable (no DB/secret). `createAuth` is now async (ADR-0366: it awaits\n   210\t// `createKyselyAdapter` to build the session-token-wrapped adapter), so the cache holds the\n   211\t// in-flight/settled PROMISE itself, not its result — every caller `await`s the same one.\n   212\tlet cached: Promise<AuthInstance | null> | undefined;\n   213\t\n   214\t/**\n   215\t * The process-wide better-auth instance, or `null` when the runtime is not configured for\n   216\t * sign-in (`DATABASE_URL` or `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` absent). Callers MUST treat `null` as \"sign-in\n   217\t * unavailable\" — the route handler answers 503, `getSession` returns no session. Resolved once and\n   218\t * cached (one Postgres pool per process).\n   219\t */\n   220\texport function getAuth(): Promise<AuthInstance | null> {\n   221\t  if (cached !== undefined) return cached;\n   222\t  const url = process.env.DATABASE_URL?.trim();\n   223\t  const secret = process.env.BETTER_AUTH_SECRET?.trim();\n   224\t  if (\n   225\t    url === undefined ||\n   226\t    url.length === 0 ||\n   227\t    secret === undefined ||\n   228\t    secret.length === 0\n   229\t  ) {\n   230\t    cached = Promise.resolve(null);\n   231\t    return cached;\n   232\t  }\n   233\t  const hmacKey = process.env.SESSION_TOKEN_HMAC_KEY?.trim();\n   234\t  if (hmacKey === undefined || hmacKey.length === 0) {\n   235\t    // Fail-closed (ADR-0366): DATABASE_URL + BETTER_AUTH_SECRET ARE configured (this would\n   236\t    // otherwise be a live auth runtime), so a missing HMAC key is an operator misconfiguration,\n   237\t    // never a silent \"sign-in unavailable\" degrade or a raw-token fallback. Throwing here surfaces\n   238\t    // loudly (a crashed boot / a failed health check) instead of masking a forgotten env var as an\n   239\t    // ordinary DB-down outage.\n   240\t    throw new Error(\n   241\t      \"SESSION_TOKEN_HMAC_KEY is required once DATABASE_URL/BETTER_AUTH_SECRET are configured (ADR-0366) — refusing to start auth with raw session-token storage.\",\n   242\t    );\n   243\t  }\n   244\t  const pool = createPgPool(url);\n   245\t  cached = createAuth({\n   246\t    database: pool,\n   247\t    secret,\n   248\t    emailer: resolveEmailer(),\n   249\t    hmacKey,\n   250\t    baseURL: process.env.BETTER_AUTH_URL?.trim(),\n   251\t  });\n   252\t  return cached;\n   253\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
