| Where                                                                                                                |\n | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n | Board fork-walk D1–D15, full walk (2026-08-09)                          | All 15 rows of `outputs/audit/2026-07-board/BOARD-REPORT.md` §3 disposed in picker rounds, each re-verified against current state first (full record: `outputs/audit/2026-07-board/WALK-CAPTURE.md`). Locks: **$1,649 Compliance FINAL, adjustment window closed** (0403, re-asked against the operative ADR-0386 number) · **discounted close never = list-price validation** (0404, supersedes 0391 §D5 at an explicit conflict re-ask) · **seller plane stays, Python frozen at two islands** (0405, confirms 0009/0096/0105/0206) · **one launch gate: truth-fixes + four receipts + rails, outreach held behind it, tripwire arms at launch** (0406, supersedes 0391 §D15 in part). Dispositions: D3 site stays public with the two D1 claims standing (accepted risk) · D9 REOPENED → audit delivered (#423: 18 verified + 6 decision-gated cuts; operator picker round pending) · D11 one legal re-verify pass before close · D12 message-match executed (#420, merged + deployed 2026-08-10) · ADR-0391's three instruments + D13 interview spec stand.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | ADR-0403; ADR-0404; ADR-0405; ADR-0406                                                                               |\n | Reconcile picker · agent-usage registry premise (2026-08-09)            | ADR-0399's registry clause assumed never-published; the ledger is truth and carries 11 gate-attested rows through 0.2.9 (published-never-sold). Operator re-locked **delist + fold, this wave**: ADR-0271 module-level delist row appended (provenance retained), index rebuilt 54→53, code folded to agent-trajectory `./usage`, package deleted, census 59 packages / 75 workspaces. Executed at reconcile.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  | ADR-0402 (supersedes 0399 §3)                                                                                        |\n | Ponytail-audit remediation picker (2026-08-09)                          | Two picker rounds over the 42-finding repo-wide audit (29 confirmed / 5 downgraded / 0 refuted, adversarially verified). **The headline chain deletes** — five undeployed reference apps + the two remaining dissolved edition metas, apps/base's four integration tests relocated first, registry ledger append-only (0397) · **verify-pack publishes with the NEXT train as published-never-sold** — the picker's bundle-member phrasing corrected to ADR-0385's no-membership lock; membership stays a separate catalog/pricing fork (0398) · **agent-usage folds into agent-trajectory `./usage`** — re-litigating the July t4-memo KEEP with the operator (0399) · **the site demo surface splits THIS wave, multi-zone shape** — new `apps/demos` on `/demos/*` rewrite, same-origin iframes, Railway service creation operator-paged (0400) · **sweep locks** — three bundle ledes rewrite to real members, platform-reads becomes canonical read-SQL home (fold-into-service rejected: sold package), audit-harness + demo-registry → `tooling/`, mechanical cut list executes fork-free (0401). Execution: five clustered PRs, ADRs ride PR 1.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | ADR-0397–0401                                                                                                        |\n | D5 · discounted-close evidence (2026-07-26)                             | **One 40%-off design-partner close counts as list-price validation**, against the re-walk's HIGH-confidence recommendation to keep list-reaction and discounted-conversion ledgers separate. The single commercial instrument therefore cannot isolate discount sensitivity or support a full-price-elasticity claim; a future claim needs a new instrument.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | ADR-0391                                                                                                             |\n | D6 · bounded-thesis tripwire (2026-07-26)                               | Run one bounded cycle under the current design-partner thesis. Binding tripwire: **\"zero paid partners at day 30 stops further product spend and reopens the wedge or pivot board\"**. D5 means one 40%-off close clears it, an easier bar than the re-walk assumed; the wedge gets neither an early pivot nor indefinite protection.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | ADR-0391                                                                                                             |\n | D7 · three demand instruments (2026-07-26)                              | **Three instruments, against the re-walk's four-instrument recommendation**: D13 economic-buyer map first; one commercial instrument carrying D5's merged list/discount label; public developer distribution with its own denominator. The commercial leg inherits D5's full-price blind spot.                                     