not a Caisson deadline. Publish in a new first-party **`/writing` collection inside `apps/site`**, chosen over the separately recommended compliance-docs MDX page and off-site-only publication. The separate surface lane now shares the six-day delivery window; it is not built in this PR.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | ADR-0391; ADR-0390                                                                                                   |\n | D13 · economic-buyer map (2026-07-26)                                   | Interview **three to five economic buyers or procurement actors**, excluding a developer-only panel; capture budget authority, procurement path, self-serve tolerance, and auditor involvement. This adds targeted recruiting and calendar time before commercial interpretation instead of assuming developer proximity equals buying authority.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | ADR-0391                                                                                                             |\n | D15 · separate learning and revenue clocks (2026-07-26)                 | Learning starts after D10's four technical receipts and reaches full exposure through interviews plus five outbound emails. Revenue starts only after auditor acceptance, a real Paddle-to-Mercury transaction path, and a **written cost-to-serve bar** for support, security, and auditor assistance; that missing bar is now a gating deliverable.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          | ADR-0391                                                                                                             |\n | Launch-readiness and Blacksmith-cost locks (2026-07-26)                 | Four operator locks: **Article 50 content verifies now and publishes by 2026-08-01** (2026-08-02 is legal applicability, not a Caisson deadline; `/writing` surface recorded by ADR-0391) · **Ask-AI arming = runbook rows plus a presence-only configured probe**, not site-wide boot failure · **Paddle sandbox drift gets a GET-only audit before cleanup**, with no archive/delete/reprice in this act · **Blacksmith accepts ~$79/month, alert $120, revisit after launch**, superseding PF2-1's ~$4-8 assumption on 9,805 4-vCPU-minutes / $66.35 due / $79.11 projected; GitHub-hosted is not cheaper for this private Free-plan repository.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            | ADR-0390                                                                                                             |\n | Full-state completion program (2026-07-25)                              | Reconcile repository/work/deployment truth first; make dependency-cruiser prove TypeScript coverage; make price authority total over sellable commercial modules; split limiter failure policy (Paddle webhook fail-open + alert, issuer/admin/eval fail-closed 503); reconcile the fleet to one immutable SHA behind the external-system/data-migration gate; complete only verified residuals from existing locked plans; build Inngest v4, Azure Key Vault, and Azure Blob WORM adapters; preserve public-marketing + CF-gated commerce, $1,449 Compliance, unchanged buyer copy, two Python services, and the frozen LLM/agent families; run one release after all code waves.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             | ADR-0379; `outputs/specs/full-state-completion/SPEC.md`                                                              |\n | oscal-spine price and Compliance reprice (2026-07-25)                   | Successor to ADR-0382 lock 3, carrying the number that ADR deliberately deferred. **`oscal-spine` lists at $249**, matching `frameworks-pack` — the package it is carved from and whose fifth crosswalk axis it is. **It joins Compliance's `members`** (all ten current members are compliance capabilities; the membership join date drives ADR-0257 snapshot grandfathering, and there are zero buyers). **Compliance reprices $1,449 → $1,649**, SUPERSEDING ADR-0381 lock 2's hold: the bundle sits at 70.0% of member subtotal today, the enlarged subtotal is $2,319, and $1,649 is the nearest committed X49 figure to that band at 71.1%. Below-sum invariant holds ($1,649 < $2,319). Execution is a dedicated wave — the price-authority gate fails on a partial change, so every surface moves at once: package carve first, then pricebook, the 35/66 → 36/68 catalog, registry index, ~10 price surfaces, the docs-RAG and support-bot answers, and the state docs. Not started this sitting; four branches are open and ADR-0328 calls a reconcile at two or more. ADR-0383.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    | ADR-0383                                                                                                             |\n | oscal-spine carve boundary, license, and renewal knock-on (2026-07-25)  | Successor closing ADR-0383’s two “Not decided here” items plus a third question ADR-0383 never asked. **Carve boundary:** the WHOLE OSCAL surface moves to `@caisson/oscal-spine` — not just the ADR-0363/0364 spine — and BOTH `frameworks-pack` and `compliance-core` depend on it and re-export it, so no consumer breaks (`apps/compliance`’s `toOscalBundle` import keeps resolving) and neither parent needs a major bump. Operator pick, overriding the spine-only recommendation. The accepted trade, recorded: a $299 compliance-core buyer receives the $249 package through the re-export, so the standalone SKU addresses buyers of neither parent and the bundle delivers it directly to Compliance buyers. **License:** `LicenseRef-Caisson-Commercial` — forced, not chosen: ADR-0094’s open Base is Apache-2.0 AND free, so a $249 SKU cannot sit in it, and all five sibling compliance packages are commercial. Parent→spine is a sideways module-tier dep, not a depend-up. **Renewals:** no number set — ADR-0260 §5’s flat-40%-X9 `renewalAmount` already derives every row. oscal-spine = **$99**; standard 1-year tenor, `years` unset, multi-year lever stays unarmed. Knock-on ADR-0383 missed: the $1,649 reprice moves the **Compliance renewal $579 → $659**, and `tools/paddle-catalog-recreate.ts:439`’s `57900` assertion becomes `65900`. Operator picked letting the formula run over pinning $579, which would have made every renewal a hand-maintained number. RENEWAL_BOOK 32 → 33 rows, confirming the 35/66 → 36/68 count (one product, two prices).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    | ADR-0384                                                                                                             |\n | Evidence-pack verifier and export redaction (2026-07-25)                | Two locks from the grill-remediation picker, both on the evidence-export path this product sells. **Verifier:** the pack ships NO executable verifier — an embedded one cannot establish its own integrity, and the seal covered receipts but not `verify.mjs`, whose substitution the unsigned top-level digest could not prevent. A new commercial `@caisson/verify-pack` becomes the only sanctioned path, and the seal extends over a canonical file manifest so any in-archive substitution breaks the signature. Operator pick, overriding the recommendation to keep a bundled convenience verifier. Honest limitation recorded in the ADR: `npm publish` is operator-gated, so the out-of-band guarantee is a design property until publish and the docs must not imply the package is already installable. It is a verification TOOL, not a sellable SKU — no `SKU_RETAIL` row, no bundle membership, no catalog-count change, and no interaction with the ADR-0383/0384 wave. **Redaction:** exports move from a 14-name exact-match denylist — which missed `credential(s)`, `auth`, `clientAssertion`, and `setCookie` (that last one normalises to `setcookie` and never matched the listed `cookie`), returning plaintext secrets server-side — to a fail-closed per-event allowlist: a field no schema names is dropped, and an event type with no schema exports nothing at all. Operator pick, matching the recommendation, over broadening the list, because a denylist can only redact what someone predicted. The broadened denylist is retained as display-side defense in depth.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | ADR-0385                                                                                                             |\n | Everything reprice, release sequencing, wave force-push (2026-07-25)    | Three locks from the reconcile picker. **Everything → $2,259** (+$200): ADR-0384 hands the whole-catalog bundle a new $249 SKU, and NO gate objects — the below-sum lock gets easier as the member sum grows and the price ladder only needs Everything ≥ Compliance — so left alone its premium over Compliance would have narrowed $610 → $410 with every check green. +$200 matches the treatment Compliance got for the same $249 of content. Carries `renewalAmount(\"everything\")` $819 → $899 by the ADR-0260 §5 formula, plus the `PRICE_AUTHORITY` cents row and the display sheet. **Sequencing:** deploy the fleet AND cut the release tag now off the reconciled main, with a second train after the oscal wave — operator pick over the recommendation to hold the tag. Accepted cost: two release+deploy cycles and a first tag whose pricebook knowingly advertises the superseded $1,449/$2,059; `npm publish` should therefore wait for the second train. **Force-push:** `--force-with-lease` on any `feature/*` branch during a reconcile wave is pre-authorized and no longer pages (`main` never is), because rebasing onto a squash-merged main is the wave's normal path; the standing trap — a rebased child loses its base changesets from `--since=origin/main` — rides with the grant.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               | ADR-0386                                                                                                             |\n | Field-crypto production backing and the deploy arming pass (2026-07-25) | Four locks taken to unblock the fleet deploy. **Backing:** Azure Key Vault KMS backs field-crypto in production, operator pick over the ADR-0043 derived env pair — the master key never sits in a Railway variable and crypto-shred becomes an act on the KMS. **Ordering:** the async refactor lands BEFORE the deploy, operator pick over deploying on the derived pair first, because `KmsKeyProvider` implements the async-only `FieldKeyProvider` while both production consumers (`apps/site/lib/byok.ts:137`, `packages/ai-kit/src/mcp-run-tools.ts:61`) require `SyncFieldKeyProvider` — KMS is a code wave through the tenant-secret path, not an environment swap. A sync caching shim is explicitly REJECTED: resident plaintext DEKs would negate the property that motivated KMS. The one-way door is the first real buyer BYOK seal, not this deploy, so the lock buys ordering rather than optionality. **Arming:** a full pre-deploy pass over all six legs plus atomic rotation of the three byte-identical shared bearers, not a one-variable fix — the BYOK pair reached a launch runbook unrecorded, which is evidence of a class. **Unrecorded values:** adopt and record, never regenerate; BYOK ciphertext has no recovery path.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       | ADR-0387                                                                                                             |\n | KMS async boundary and request key lifetime (2026-07-25)                | The field-crypto KMS context **prefetches every key version from 1 through current at request bind**, preserving ADR-0043's no-remigration invariant while keeping `sealField`/`openField` synchronous. The accepted cost is O(rotation count) Azure unwraps and request-local plaintext residency. Production binds through a wrapper that zeroizes every DEK buffer in `finally`; partial prefetch failure zeroizes completed unwraps and fails closed with no derived/DEMO fallback. ~~**Provision on first seal**, not tenant creation~~ — **superseded by ADR-0392 §3: provisioning happens at context bind, including for read-only callers**, because a bind reads the current key version first; concurrent binds elect one append-only version-1 winner, zeroize the loser's generated plaintext, and use the winner without overwriting it. Prefetch depth is capped per ADR-0392 §2.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | ADR-0389                                                                                                             |\n | Upgrade-credit floor, tag signing, oscal-spine SKU (2026-07-25)         | Three-question picker over the remaining fork rows. **The paid amount lives on the entitlement grant, written at grant time** — a correction rides this lock: `order_record` has stored `amount` since migration 0019, so money storage was never absent; what was missing is a PER-SKU amount, since `order_record.amount` is the transaction total and cannot be split across a cart afterwards. New nullable `charged_amount`/`charged_currency` (minor units) on `entitlement_grant` as tail migration `0031`, stamped only when the line's charge is genuinely one SKU's price (quantity 1, non-zero, single entitlement); `resolveUpgradeCredit` returns `max(retail, paid)` rounding UP, and the paid map is an argument so the pricebook stays DB-free. Timing is the substance: zero buyers means no backfill, and after the first sale the per-SKU amount is unrecoverable. **Release tags signed going forward** (SSH), readiness check 0b advisory because an existing tag cannot become signed without the very mutation the signature prevents. **`oscal-spine` becomes a priced SKU** — direction only; the number, the package carve out of `frameworks-pack` + `compliance-core`, and the 35/66 catalog change are owed a successor ADR. ADR-0382.                                                                                                                                                      