{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_71","type":"agent_message","text":"Two release-blocking defects are now proven. First, the R4 artifact contract is self-referential: the tagged commit must contain a file naming that same commit’s SHA, but adding those bytes changes the SHA. Second, the new server checkout uses the dashboard session resolver that deliberately converts account-membership read failures into the personal account, so a selected organization purchase can still be checked and stamped against the wrong tenant. I’m completing the remaining changed-file sweep and documenting the exact closure matrix and verification limits."}}
